// A const param read as a value inside a string interpolation. `${F}` and `${F:x}` both route through
// holeBuiltinType, which asks receiverTypeNode for the hole's type — a path that knew about locals and
// fields but not about a bound const param, so a formatted hole reported "base specifier `:x` applies
// only to an integer hole" about something that plainly was one.
fn int32 widths() comptime(int32 F) {
    string d = "${F}";
    string h = "${F:x}";
    int32 n = 0;
    if (d == "255")  { n = n + 1; }
    if (h == "ff")   { n = n + 1; }
    return n;
}
fn int32 main() { return widths()#(255); }   // 2
